{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c355","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a08726-461e-70c2-b068-84ac73bce259"},"sequence":5,"recorded_at":1780531400000005,"record_type":"status","durability":"ephemeral","causation_id":"5377e6ac-7afb-4885-bf43-dcc6aa311a62","payload_type":"turn.input.user","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"turn_input_user","command_id":"5377e6ac-7afb-4885-bf43-dcc6aa311a62","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5377e6ac-7afb-4885-bf43-dcc6aa311a62"},"prompt":"# Agent Task Assignment\n\n## FIRST — Run Immediately\n\n```bash\ntask-board m 'set_status(TASK-260908-2tkufa, status=development)'\n```\n\n## Operational Constraints (Headless Run)\n\n- Never background a long command and end your turn: a headless session ends with\n  the turn and the process dies with it, while the run is still recorded as\n  completed with no evidence attached.\n- A single shell call is time-bounded (~10 minutes). Split long checks into\n  bounded sequential calls (package subsets, `-run` masks) and state explicitly\n  what you reran yourself versus accepted from already-attached evidence.\n- Attach evidence before you end the lifecycle, not after: \"I will attach it when\n  the run finishes\" is unfulfillable by construction.\n\n## Role Contract\n\n- **Role:** `developer` (`implementer`) — Writes code, fixes bugs, writes tests\n- Obey task scope, acceptance criteria, and checklist.\n- Report real exit codes; failing gates stay failing.\n- Use compact task-specific board projections; skip routine `summary()`,\n  `plan()`, `schema()`, and `{ full }`. Request scoped schema only after an\n  unknown call.\n- Load only relevant and explicitly required skills.\n\n### Skills\n\n- `project-management`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/SKILL.md`\n- `swiftui`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/swiftui/SKILL.md`\n- `core-data`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/core-data/SKILL.md`\n- `go-testing-tools`: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.claude/skills/go-testing-tools/SKILL.md`\n- `architecture-diagrams`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/architecture-diagrams/SKILL.md`\n\n### Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] Actual catalogue, registry, CI and traceability consumers use the approved v0.6.0 source with regenerated artifacts and consumer-entry positive and stale-authority refusal tests.\n- [ ] Every new selector, authentication, credential and migration obligation maps to its real owner without claiming unimplemented runtime support; historical authority remains explicit and valid.\n- [ ] Repository local tests, coverage and required gates pass with per-command evidence; mutation claims include valid instrumentation controls and semantic failures; reviewed task-board CR is published.\n- [ ] Code written per task description and AC\n- [ ] Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\n- [ ] In a managed Story worktree the candidate is left UNCOMMITTED in the worktree for the handoff to snapshot — never commit on the Story branch. A producer commit moves the branch tip off the recorded checkpoint and the handoff refuses with change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint; repair with `git reset --soft <checkpoint_oid>` before completing again.\n- [ ] Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio — `n of m AC rows driven` — and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\n- [ ] Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\n- [ ] Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant — the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\n- [ ] A gate that inspects source text is additionally attacked by a mutant that PRESERVES the searched-for token and changes behavior, and the mutant harness executes the behavioral suite, not only the static checker.\n- [ ] Lint clean\n- [ ] Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\n- [ ] New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\n- [ ] Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\n\n## Task\n\n- **ID:** TASK-260908-2tkufa\n- **Title:** TASK-260908-2tkufa: bind-approved-contract-catalog-and-implementation-owners\n- **Parent:** STORY-260908-18woqo\n\n### Description\n\nRegenerate and reconcile contract catalog, traceability ownership and source-version validation after the approved normative pin is adopted. Every added or refined selector/auth/migration obligation must map to its real implementation owner; unsupported new runtime behavior must not be reported as implemented. Preserve acceptance evidence for unchanged legacy contracts and resume the existing dependent leaves after this Story lands.\n\n### Scope\n\ninternal/catalog, internal/traceability, directly required generator checks and board scope bindings; no edits to another Story partial implementation.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n\nFull contract census and source references match the adopted normative source; existing and added contract obligations have non-duplicated real owners; generator/traceability gates pass and detect omissions; legacy support claims remain truthful; exact reviewed signed Story delivered before unblocking dependent code.\n\n## Instructions\n\n### TASK-260908-2tkufa_primary-implementation.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260908-2tkufa/TASK-260908-2tkufa_primary-implementation.md`\n\n- Byte count: `2872`\n- Content digest: `sha256:18056889cac34939b74b635089b64684a9af12024a5e538a6982a05fc7d84126`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n\n\n## Evidence and Safety\n\n- Add/update a task-scoped outcome named `TASK-260908-2tkufa_*` before handoff:\n  `task-board m 'add_resource(TASK-260908-2tkufa, name=TASK-260908-2tkufa_results.md, content=\"...\", type=outcome, description=\"Handoff evidence\")'`\n- Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior ships with negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject; prove the bound by narrowing it, not only by deleting it, and name the production call site. Shapes and incidents: `references/negative-evidence.md`.\n- An absence and a failure to read are different facts; report unknown instead of inferring a property from a proxy signal.\n- Stop-The-Line only for an evidence-backed external blocker or unresolved human-only product/platform/architecture/approval decision. Persist evidence, failed attempts, options/tradeoffs, recommendation, and exact input needed; otherwise rework autonomously.\n- `to-review` is a role handoff, not accepted completion. Report **ready for review** or **handed off to review**.\n\n## LAST — Run For Role Handoff\n\nAfter AC, checklist, validation, and outcome evidence:\n\n```bash\ntask-board handoff TASK-260908-2tkufa --role developer\n```\n\n## Working Directory\nBoard directory: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board`\n\nWork in the project root. Never edit board files directly.\n\n## Story Workspace\n\nYou are running in an isolated Git worktree for STORY-260908-18woqo.\n\n- Workspace path: `.temp/STORY-260908-18woqo/worktree` (this is your working directory)\n- Branch: `task-board/story/STORY-260908-18woqo`, forked from `main`\n- Authoritative board: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board` (already exported as `TASK_BOARD_DIR`)\n\nMake every repository change here. Do not commit, switch, rebase, merge, or delete this branch, and do not run `task-board` against the `.task-board` copy inside this worktree — it is a checkout artifact, not the board. Integration into trunk is the orchestrator's step, not yours.\n\nLeave your work UNCOMMITTED in the worktree — the handoff snapshots the working tree against the recorded checkpoint. A commit of your own on this branch is refused at handoff with `change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint`, and the repair is `git reset --soft <checkpoint_oid>` before completing again.\n"}}
